        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">A conversion field confers a 4+ Invulnerable save.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Enhanced Data-tether" id="2a57-2bb7-62e9-9e20" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">Whenever a unit with an enhanced data-tether is affected by a Doctrina Imperative, all models in the unit add 1 to their Leadership characteristic until the start of your next turn. Note this is not cumulative with the effects of a Broad Spectrum Data-tether.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Infoslave Skull" id="624c-fa17-905d-cc3b" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">A model equipped with an Infoslave skull adds 1 to its Leadership and gains the Acute Senses special rule.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Omnispex" id="54b2-7035-786b-485e" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">Cover saves taken against attacks made by a unit with this equipment are made with a -1 modifier.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Refractor Field" id="0d99-ae16-6e05-3494" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">A Refractor Field confers a 5+ Invulnerable save.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Broad Spectrum Data-tether" id="68ba-31d3-659d-8038" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">All models in friendly units within 6&quot; of at least one model with a Broad Spectrum Data-tether and are affected by a Doctrina Imperative add 1 to their Leadership characteristic on their profile until the start of your next turn. Note this is not cumulative with the effects of an enhance data-tether.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Emanatus Force Field" id="239d-e7ed-bec0-6af7" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">An emanatus force fields confers a 6+ invulnerable save.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Mindscanner Probe" id="22e1-b45a-c95f-509e" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">If a unit within 6&quot; of a friendly model equipped with a Mindscanner probe is charged, the charging model do not gain bonus Attacks from charging. However, if the target was already locked in combat from a previous turn, or has Gone to Ground, the mindscanner probe has no effect and the attackers gain bonus Attacks as normal.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="The Omniscient Mask" id="8016-000f-0198-8433" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">The bearer of the Omniscient Mask has the Fearless and Preferred Enemy special rule.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Pater Radium" id="02e1-c87e-77d3-0096" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">If the bearer of the Pater Radium is locked in combat with one or more enemy units at the end of the Assault phase, each of these enemy units must take a Toughness test using the Toughness value of the majority of the unit (or highest in the case of a tie). If the test is failed, the unit takes D6 randomly allocated Wounds with no Armour saves allowed.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Phosphoenix" id="8dc4-4419-47cc-fa0f" hidden="false" typeId="8e6f-7553-28c5-95a0" typeName="Weapons">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="9b9e-0c24-e409-a801">6&quot;</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Str." typeId="1ebc-896c-43de-904a">5</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="730c-47dc-fdad-3c8b">2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="1524-30c8-5da7-66ff">Pistol, Luminagen, Poisoned (3+)</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="45fd-0f50-e1d0-907c">A successful To Hit roll scores 3 hits against the target unit instead of 1.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Skull of Elder Nikola" id="dad7-64b3-24c1-74b4" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">Once per game, the bearer of the Skull of Elder Nikola can unleash its power instead of firing a weapon. To do so, roll a number of D6 equal to the current turn number; the total rolled is the range of the attack in inches. All enemy vehicles within range suffer a Strength 1 AP- hit with the Haywire special rule.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Radium Pistol" id="9cce-159e-59e3-54ae" hidden="false" typeId="8e6f-7553-28c5-95a0" typeName="Weapons">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="9b9e-0c24-e409-a801">12&quot;</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Str." typeId="1ebc-896c-43de-904a">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="730c-47dc-fdad-3c8b">5</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="1524-30c8-5da7-66ff">Pistol</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="45fd-0f50-e1d0-907c">Each roll To Wound of 6 causes 2 additional Wounds on the target unit.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Radium Jezzail" id="b438-96f0-fdab-b5cb" hidden="false" typeId="8e6f-7553-28c5-95a0" typeName="Weapons">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="9b9e-0c24-e409-a801">30&quot;</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Str." typeId="1ebc-896c-43de-904a">X</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="730c-47dc-fdad-3c8b">5</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="1524-30c8-5da7-66ff">Heavy 2, Sniper</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="45fd-0f50-e1d0-907c">Each roll To Wound of 6 causes 2 additional Wounds on the target unit.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Bulky" id="2342-e7a3-e34f-c24f" hidden="false" typeId="ccb3-7790-3139-7975" typeName="Abilities">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="e24a-6018-20cf-d76c">This counts as two models for transport capacity.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Dunestrider" id="016c-2687-c164-62e3" hidden="false" typeId="ccb3-7790-3139-7975" typeName="Abilities">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="e24a-6018-20cf-d76c">This unit adds 3&quot; to its maximum Move, Run and Charge distance.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Twin-linked Cognis Autocannon" id="7a27-c64a-5a5f-b3f0" hidden="false" typeId="8e6f-7553-28c5-95a0" typeName="Weapons">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="9b9e-0c24-e409-a801">48&quot;</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Str." typeId="1ebc-896c-43de-904a">7</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="730c-47dc-fdad-3c8b">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="1524-30c8-5da7-66ff">Heavy 2, Twin-linked</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="45fd-0f50-e1d0-907c"/>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Twin-linked Cognis Lascannon" id="2d86-bb35-4474-e59b" hidden="false" typeId="8e6f-7553-28c5-95a0" typeName="Weapons">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="9b9e-0c24-e409-a801">48&quot;</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Str." typeId="1ebc-896c-43de-904a">9</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="730c-47dc-fdad-3c8b">2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="1524-30c8-5da7-66ff">Heavy 1, Twin-linked</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="45fd-0f50-e1d0-907c"/>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Crusader" id="b43c-20bd-45d0-01b4" hidden="false" typeId="ccb3-7790-3139-7975" typeName="Abilities">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="e24a-6018-20cf-d76c">This model rolls an extra D6 when making a Run move, choosing the highest.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Twin-linked Heavy Phosphor Blaster" id="4902-b310-72ec-b225" hidden="false" typeId="8e6f-7553-28c5-95a0" typeName="Weapons">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="9b9e-0c24-e409-a801">36&quot;</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Str." typeId="1ebc-896c-43de-904a">6</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="730c-47dc-fdad-3c8b">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="1524-30c8-5da7-66ff">Heavy 3, Luminagen, Twin-linked</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="45fd-0f50-e1d0-907c"/>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Incantation of the Iron Soul" id="1092-b756-a43f-1d0c" hidden="false" typeId="4ad0-1385-d4b7-6623" typeName="Canticle of the Omnissiah">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="1-3 Units" typeId="0311-a129-4f86-3590">Friendly units with the Canticles of the Omnissiah special rule gain the Stubborn special rule.</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="4-7 Units" typeId="8f19-d77f-8273-56ae">Friendly units with the Canticles of the Omnissiah special rule gain the Stubborn special rule and may re-roll all failed Morale, Leadership and Pinning Tests.</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="8+ Units" typeId="1bf5-4c5b-a381-4550">Friendly units with the Canticles of the Omnissiah special rule gain the Fearless special rule.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Litany of the Electromancer" id="3672-fb91-df93-b466" hidden="false" typeId="4ad0-1385-d4b7-6623" typeName="Canticle of the Omnissiah">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="1-3 Units" typeId="0311-a129-4f86-3590">Enemy units suffer a single Strength 4 AP- hit for each model with the Canticles of the Omnissiah special rule in units that they are locked in combat with, resolved at Initiative 10.</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="4-7 Units" typeId="8f19-d77f-8273-56ae">Enemy units suffer two Strength 4 AP- hits for each model with the Canticles of the Omnissiah special rule in units that they are locked in combat with, resolved at Initiative 10.</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="8+ Units" typeId="1bf5-4c5b-a381-4550">Enemy units suffer three Strength 4 AP- hits for each model with the Canticles of the Omnissiah special rule in units that they are locked in combat with, resolved at Initiative 10.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Chant of the Remorseless Fist" id="adad-e1a2-bdfb-c68f" hidden="false" typeId="4ad0-1385-d4b7-6623" typeName="Canticle of the Omnissiah">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="1-3 Units" typeId="0311-a129-4f86-3590">Friendly units with the Canticles of the Omnissiah special rule re-roll failed To Hit rolls of 1 when making close combat attacks.</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="4-7 Units" typeId="8f19-d77f-8273-56ae">Friendly units with the Canticles of the Omnissiah special rule re-roll failed To Hit rolls of 1 or 2 when making close combat attacks.</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="8+ Units" typeId="1bf5-4c5b-a381-4550">Friendly units with the Canticles of the Omnissiah special rule re-roll all failed To Hit rolls when making close combat attacks.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Shroudpsalm" id="6353-55e8-7f9e-220e" hidden="false" typeId="4ad0-1385-d4b7-6623" typeName="Canticle of the Omnissiah">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="1-3 Units" typeId="0311-a129-4f86-3590">All friendly units with the Canticles of the Omnissiah special rule gain the Stealth special rule.</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="4-7 Units" typeId="8f19-d77f-8273-56ae">All friendly units with the Canticles of the Omnissiah special rule gain the Shrouded special rule.</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="8+ Units" typeId="1bf5-4c5b-a381-4550">All friendly units with the Canticles of the Omnissiah special rule gain the Stealth and Shrouded special rules.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Shrouded" id="26d3-9c9c-839c-ce72" hidden="false" typeId="ccb3-7790-3139-7975" typeName="Abilities">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="e24a-6018-20cf-d76c">A unit that contains at least one model with this special rule counts its cover save as being 2 points better than normal. Note that this means a model with the Shrouded special rule always has a cover save of at least 5+, even if it’s in the open.


Cover save bonuses from the Shrouded and Stealth special rules are cumulative (to a maximum of a 2+ cover save).</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Invocation of Machine-Might" id="a5fc-d70d-7ab4-6a0c" hidden="false" typeId="4ad0-1385-d4b7-6623" typeName="Canticle of the Omnissiah">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="1-3 Units" typeId="0311-a129-4f86-3590">Friendly units with the Canticles of the Omnissiah special rule add 1 to their Strength characteristic.</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="4-7 Units" typeId="8f19-d77f-8273-56ae">Friendly units with the Canticles of the Omnissiah special rule add 2 to their Strength characteristic.</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="8+ Units" typeId="1bf5-4c5b-a381-4550">Friendly units with the Canticles of the Omnissiah special rule add 3 to their Strength characteristic.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Benediction of Omniscience" id="9071-fe82-1508-fb2d" hidden="false" typeId="4ad0-1385-d4b7-6623" typeName="Canticle of the Omnissiah">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="1-3 Units" typeId="0311-a129-4f86-3590">Friendly units with the Canticles of the Omnissiah special rule re-roll failed To Hit rolls of 1 when making shooting attacks.</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="4-7 Units" typeId="8f19-d77f-8273-56ae">Friendly units with the Canticles of the Omnissiah special rule re-roll failed To Hit rolls of 1 or 2 when making shooting attacks.</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="8+ Units" typeId="1bf5-4c5b-a381-4550">Friendly units with the Canticles of the Omnissiah special rule re-roll failed To Hit rolls when making shooting attacks.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Stasis Field" id="8f48-4935-7f88-27c3" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">While a model equipped with a stasis field has Gone to Ground, it gains a 2+ Invulnerable save, but its Weapon Skill and Ballistic Skill characteristics are reduced to 0.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Mask of the Alpha Dominus" id="c60c-68f9-794f-0c5d" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">The bearer can use the Mask of the Alpha Dominus at any time to instantly change the Battle Protocol of a friendly Kastelan Robot Maniple or Cohort Cybernetica Formation within 12&quot; of the bearer. The new Battle Protocol becomes active immediately. However, the unit cannot use the Battle Protocol that they changed from for the rest of the battle.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Autocaduceus of Arkhan Land" id="48e9-bb19-791a-9c78" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">The bearer of this wargear gains the Eternal Warrior special rule.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Raiment of the Technomartyr" id="7515-ac3a-354c-c715" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">The Raiment of the Technomartyr confers a 2+ Armour Save.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Scryerskull Perspicatus" id="b244-2dab-b0c3-9819" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">At the start of each of your turns, a model with the Scryerskull Perspicatus can choose to scry an enemy vehicle anywhere on the battlefield. If you choose to scry a vehicle, any friendly units re-roll failed armour penetration rolls against that vehicle, and can choose to re-roll glancing hits scored on it in an attempt to instead get a penetrating hit, until the start of your next turn.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Mechadendrite Harness" id="ed4c-f542-22ef-2cfe" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">A model with a mechadendrite harness can fire all of its ranged weapons in the Shooting phase. In addition, a model with a mechadendrite harness is also equipped with a dataspike.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Carapace-mounted Incendine Combustor" id="deee-8b30-e1ac-8818" hidden="false" typeId="8e6f-7553-28c5-95a0" typeName="Weapons">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="9b9e-0c24-e409-a801">Template</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Str." typeId="1ebc-896c-43de-904a">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="730c-47dc-fdad-3c8b">5</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="1524-30c8-5da7-66ff">Assault 1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="45fd-0f50-e1d0-907c"/>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Carapace-mounted Heavy Phosphor Blaster" id="cee0-fc09-5a6b-c918" hidden="false" typeId="8e6f-7553-28c5-95a0" typeName="Weapons">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="9b9e-0c24-e409-a801">36&quot;</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Str." typeId="1ebc-896c-43de-904a">6</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="730c-47dc-fdad-3c8b">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="1524-30c8-5da7-66ff">Heavy 3, Luminagen</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="45fd-0f50-e1d0-907c"/>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Belleros Energy Cannon" id="eac2-83d9-8b85-49d7" hidden="false" typeId="8e6f-7553-28c5-95a0" typeName="Weapons">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="9b9e-0c24-e409-a801">36&quot;</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Str." typeId="1ebc-896c-43de-904a">6</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="730c-47dc-fdad-3c8b">5</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="1524-30c8-5da7-66ff">Heavy 1, Large Blast, Barrage</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="45fd-0f50-e1d0-907c"/>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Ferrumite Cannon" id="c52b-ddf8-7992-4b48" hidden="false" typeId="8e6f-7553-28c5-95a0" typeName="Weapons">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Range" typeId="9b9e-0c24-e409-a801">48&quot;</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Str." typeId="1ebc-896c-43de-904a">7</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="730c-47dc-fdad-3c8b">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Type" typeId="1524-30c8-5da7-66ff">Heavy 3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="45fd-0f50-e1d0-907c"/>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
  </sharedProfiles>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Haywire" id="0c87-5655-fece-2f72" hidden="false">
      <description>When a weapon with this special rule hits a vehicle, roll a D6 to determine the effect rather than rolling for armour penetration normally.


1 - No effect


2-5 - Glancing Hit


6 - Penetrating Hit</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Shred" id="4fa1-a665-3b4d-24fb" hidden="false">
      <description>May re-roll wound rolls for this weapon</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Concussive" id="1244-c96f-9562-ea64" hidden="false">
      <description>A model that suffers one or more unsaved Wounds from a weapon with this special rule is reduced to Initiative 1 until the end of the following Assault phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Luminagen" id="0199-0e32-fe50-964b" hidden="false">
      <description>A unit that suffers one or more unsaved Wounds, glancing or penetrating hits caused by a weapon with this special rule counts its cover saves as being 1 point worse than normal until the end of the phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Doctrina Imperatives" id="4e08-99b0-b82c-23fe" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of your Movement phase, you can choose up to one Doctrina Imperative from the list above. Protector Imperatives will increase the army&apos;s abilities in the Shooting phase, while Conqueror Imperatives will make the army more proficient in the Assault phase. Unless otherwise stated, each Doctrina Imperative can only be used once during the game.


Protector Imperatives: Binharic Omniscience (Alpha), Gundrill Symbiosis (Beta), Hazard Optimisation (Gamma)


Conqueror Imperatives: Hyperaction Protocols (Alpha), Technomartyr Concords (Beta), Mindstate Secutor (Gamma)</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hazard Optimisation (Gamma)" id="d7fb-ef06-3e53-a745" hidden="false">
      <description>Until the start of your next turn, all models in friendly units with the Doctrina Imperatives special rule add 1 to their Ballistic Skill characteristic.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Gundrill Symbiosis (Beta)" id="edf4-1915-24ba-51de" hidden="false">
      <description>Until the start of your next tuen, all models in friendly units with the Doctrina Imperatives special rule add 2 to their Ballistic Skill characteristic, but subtract 1 from their Weapon Skill characteristic.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Binharic Omniscience (Alpha)" id="1e11-51fc-69b3-eeaf" hidden="false">
      <description>Until the start of your next turn, all models in friendly units with the Doctrina Imperatives special rule add 3 to their Ballistic Skill characteristic, but subtract 2 from their Weapon Skill characteristic.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mindstate Secutor (Gamma)" id="8b98-91fe-8335-ffca" hidden="false">
      <description>Until the start of your next turn, all models in friendly units with the Doctrina Imperatives special rule add 1 to their Weapon Skill characteristic.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Technomartyr Concords (Beta)" id="a7aa-9da1-5e56-23b5" hidden="false">
      <description>Until the start of your next turn, all models in friendly units with the Doctrina Imperatives special rule add 2 to their Weapon Skill characteristic, but subtract 1 from their Ballistic Skill characteristic.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hyperaction Protocols (Alpha)" id="adb1-33b2-dd96-c0b9" hidden="false">
      <description>Until the start of your next turn, all models in friendly units with the Doctrina Imperatives special rule add 3 to their Weapon Skill characteristic, but subtract 2 from their Ballistic Skill characteristic.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Canticles of the Omnissiah" id="d62e-4312-059e-34ed" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of each of your turns, you can choose one Canticle of the Omnissiah from the list below. The effects of each Canticle last until the start of your next turn. Unless otherwise stated, each Canticle can only be used once during the game.


Furthermore, the strength of each Canticle will vary according to the number of units performing it. At the start of your turn, add up the number of friendly units on the battlefield that have the Canticles of the Omnissiah special rule and apply the appropriate level of effect. Do not include units that are currently Falling Back in this total. Once a Canticle has been activated it remains at that level of effect until the beginning of your next turn, even if the number of units performing it changes during that turn.


Canticles: Incantation of the Iron Soul, Litany of the Electromancer, Chant of the Remorseless Fist, Shroudpsalm, Invocation of Machine-Might, Benediction of Omniscience</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Conqueror Protocol" id="c27a-b834-9d63-318d" hidden="false">
      <description>All Kastelan Robots in the unit double their Attacks characteristic, but cannot make shooting attacks of any kind.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Aegis Protocol" id="87c6-f496-0116-d8df" hidden="false">
      <description>All Kastelan Robots in the unit have the Feel No Pain special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Protector Protocol" id="4f41-94c7-02ed-d6d7" hidden="false">
      <description>All Kastelan Robots in the unit can fire their carapace-mounted weapons twice, but cannot move under any circumstances.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
